cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying preprint (see preferred-citation)."
title: "CMC-VAE: Cross-Modal Causal Variational Autoencoder"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/goodarzilab/CrossModalCausal-VAE"
abstract: >-
  CMC-VAE learns a network linking genes and surface proteins from paired single-cell RNA and protein
  (CITE-seq) profiles. Separate encoders map each modality to exogenous latent variables, a linear latent
  structural causal model with four gated blocks (RNA to RNA, RNA to protein, protein to RNA, protein to
  protein) connects them, and linear decoders project every latent connection onto measured genes and
  proteins. This repository contains the model, training code, released weights and the scripts that
  reproduce the analyses and figures of the accompanying preprint.
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - CITE-seq
  - multi-omics
  - causal inference
  - variational autoencoder
  - structural causal model
  - gene regulatory networks
  - perturbation prediction
